# Cloudflare Pages quirks (doc/redirects_en.md): a wildcard REWRITE shadows the
# static asset tree (an old `/products/* / 200` served the homepage shell for 255
# of 269 sitemap URLs — a wildcard cannot be made to lose to a static file, so
# exact rules only, for paths with no prerendered sibling). `/index.html` is
# never a valid target: a wildcard rule is dropped silently, an exact rule
# 308-redirects to "/" and loses the path — target "/". A source matches ONLY the
# form written, so "/compare" leaves "/compare/" 404ing: every root needs both
# forms. Pages rejects the "200!" suffix. Rules match top-down; the cap is
# ~120 lines and the overflow is dropped in silence (guard MAX_LINES=100).
# Retired-URL 301s do NOT live here — they are owned by the Worker
# (backend/api/worker/src/legacyRedirects.generated.ts, mirrored from
# dist/data/legacy-redirects.json by scripts/sync_redirects_to_worker.mjs).
# A fallback for unknown sub-paths is not expressible at all (a wildcard cannot
# lose to a static file). Guard: npm run check:redirects.
/api/* https://store.balancebiketoddler.com/api/:splat 307
# Bare app roots: SPA-only routes with no prerendered sibling, so the shell
# needs an explicit exact rewrite. Do NOT widen these to wildcards — that is
# the shape that shadowed 255 prerendered pages (see the precedence note above).
# Both URL forms get their own rule: Pages matches the source exactly, so
# "/compare" alone leaves "/compare/" on the 404 page. Target "/", never
# "/index.html" (see the 308 note above). Guard: npm run check:redirects.
/compare / 200
/compare/ / 200
# /auth is a real prerendered page now (scripts/prerender-pages.ts) — no rewrite.
/search / 200
/search/ / 200
/transparency / 200
/transparency/ / 200

# Paths that outside links still point at. Each one answers 404 today, and a
# 404 on a URL somebody linked to is a lost visit and a lost signal. Both URL
# forms get their own rule: Pages matches the source exactly, so "/blog" alone
# leaves "/blog/" on the 404 page (see the exact-match note above).
/blog /news 301
/blog/ /news 301
/shop /products 301
/shop/ /products 301
/contact /about 301
/contact/ /about 301
/privacy /transparency 301
/privacy/ /transparency 301

# Chinese edition is PARTIAL: only /zh/guides and /zh/news (hubs + articles that
# have a zh body) are real prerendered pages. Every other /zh/<path> has no
# Chinese edition and would 404 if requested. Redirect those to their English
# counterpart so the language switch / manual entry never strands a visitor.
# IMPORTANT: do NOT widen these to a single "/zh/* /:splat 301" — that wildcard
# would shadow the real /zh/guides and /zh/news prerendered pages (see the
# precedence note at the top of this file). Scope each non-edition section.
/zh / 301
/zh/ / 301
/zh/transparency /transparency 301
/zh/transparency/ /transparency/ 301
/zh/transparency/* /transparency/:splat 301
/zh/reviews /reviews 301
/zh/reviews/ /reviews/ 301
/zh/reviews/* /reviews/:splat 301
/zh/products /products 301
/zh/products/ /products/ 301
/zh/products/* /products/:splat 301
/zh/about /about 301
/zh/about/ /about/ 301
/zh/compare /compare 301
/zh/compare/ /compare/ 301
/zh/search /search 301
/zh/search/ /search/ 301

